  "text": "101. Atpresent, which of the following is the correct proposition as regards the specific performance\nof a contract:\n(A) As a general rule, the specific performance of a contract is now a general remedy.\n(B) As a general rule, the specific performance of a contract is enforced by the court when\nthere exists no standard for ascertaining actual damage caused by the non-performance\nof the act agreed to be done.\n(C) As a general rule, the specific performance of a contract is enforced by the court when\nthe act agreed to be done is such that compensation in money for its non-performance\nwould not afford adequate relief.\n(D) Both (B) and (C).",
